# sweep: --bare --seed-root examples/chat/fixtures/cut-short
# A reply that reached its length limit, saved before a restart, seeded in
# place of the default conversation. The route stops before Continue is
# tapped, so nothing is sent.
wait-for Chat
wait-for so the flour can
expect Continue the answer
clean
shot continue-after-restart
# Back from the reader's keyboard returns to the reply, Continue intact.
tap Type
wait-for Type a message
clean
shot compose
tap Back
expect Continue the answer
# Continue asks for the rest in the reader's name. With no key installed the
# request is refused before it leaves, and the refusal names the command.
tap Continue the answer
wait-for Continue where you stopped.
wait-for Try again
expect kobo secret set openai
expect-missing Continue the answer
clean
shot continue-no-key
# Looking at the keyboard and backing out changes nothing, so the question
# that was never answered still offers Try again.
tap Type
wait-for Type a message
tap Back
wait-for Continue where you stopped.
expect Try again
